cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its released artifacts, please cite this
  repository using the metadata below. No paper DOI or arXiv identifier has
  been assigned yet.
title: "Microfluidic Native Physics: Reliability Audits and Physics-Guided Constraints"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Zhiyuan
repository-code: "https://github.com/LibertychaserUS/microfluidic-native-physics"
repository-artifact: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/Chaser111/microfluidic-native-physics"
url: "https://github.com/LibertychaserUS/microfluidic-native-physics"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible public-data studies of reliability under chemistry shift in
  droplet microfluidics, including a sealed-label negative validation and a
  native-variable physics-guided constrained regression protocol. The work is
  retrospective and does not claim wet-lab feasibility.
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - microfluidics
  - droplet generation
  - machine learning
  - distribution shift
  - physics-guided regression
  - applicability domain
  - conformal prediction
